{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"What is a container in computing?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"A container packages an application with its dependencies so it runs consistently across environments, isolated from the host OS."}],"category":"tech-explain"}
{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Explain what a CPU is in one sentence."},{"role":"assistant","content":"A CPU is the main processor that executes the instructions a computer runs."}],"category":"tech-explain"}
{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"What does SSH stand for?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Secure Shell — a protocol for encrypted remote access to machines."}],"category":"tech-explain"}
{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"What is a REST API?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"A REST API is an HTTP-based interface where clients request resources using standard methods like GET and POST."}],"category":"tech-explain"}
{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"How do I create a new file called notes.txt?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Run `touch notes.txt` in your shell, or create it in your editor and save."}],"category":"howto"}
{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"How do I see what processes are running?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Run `ps aux` on Linux/macOS or `tasklist` on Windows."}],"category":"howto"}
{"messages":[{"role":"user","content":"How do I check disk space?"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Run `df -h` on Linux/macOS to see filesystem usage in human-readable form."}],"category":"howto"}
